.SH NAME
DocumentType.remove \- DocumentType: remove() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]remove()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]DocumentType\f[R]
interface removes the \f[CR]DocumentType\f[R] node from its parent node.
Nothing happens if \f[CR]parentNode\f[R] is \f[CR]null\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
remove()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using \f[CR]remove()\f[R]
.IP
.EX
document.doctype; \f[I]// \(dq<!doctype html>\(aq\f[R]
document.doctype.remove();
document.doctype; \f[I]// null\f[R]
.EE
